      "message": "Calling connectToCell here is confusing, because connectToCell *requests* cell data. It\u0027s used to ensure the device brings up cell even if the device has a better network, like wifi. If the device has no wifi and has working cell data, it will switch to cell regardless. So it\u0027s not needed here.\n\nI think the test would be better if it just waits for the default network to change to non-null, and then checks that the new default network is the underlying network. Then you could remove the disconnectFromCell cleanup step.",
