      "writtenOn": "2021-12-13T15:00:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this class really needed? It doesn\u0027t do anything except provide a thread to run a callback on. There are already running threads you can use for this. For example, you could just use ConnectivityThread or you could use the main thread.\n\nSomething like \"new Handler(ConnectivityThread.getInstanceLooper())\" or \"new Handler(Looper.getMainLooper())\".\n\nConnectivityThread has the advantage that it is the same thread which runs callbacks that specify no handler. The main thread has the advantage that it runs on the same thread that by default runs lots of other callbacks (though those are not typically used in our tests).\n\nThis CtsCallbackHandlerThread has neither of those properties so it seems strictly worse than choosing one of the two.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 22,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "95814691798ab1e17249ab03090a0f4034b3438d",
