      "writtenOn": "2021-12-15T14:19:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why can\u0027t you use ConnectivityThread? This code has access to @hide methods, doesn\u0027t it?\n\nIf I\u0027m reading Jean\u0027s comment correctly, he didn\u0027t suggest adding a new CtsCallbackHandlerThread class. I think the suggested passing in a handler. That seems like a better option than adding this class.\n\nIf you do really need another thread, then I think it\u0027s better for it to be a private implementation detail of CtsNetUtils (i.e., created by CtsNetUtils and used only there) instead of a public class like CtsCallbackHandlerThread.\n\nI don\u0027t think it\u0027s a good idea to use a single thread for all callbacks in all our CTS tests because it reduces the opportunity for our tests to find race conditions.",
